+# Reduce price for rentals of 3+ days by 10%
+
+## Goal
+
+Reward customers who stay longer: a rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price. Quotes and
+bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## Scope
+
+Changes the pricing in `src/index.ts`, used by `quote` and `book`:
+
+- A period of 3 or more whole days has its total reduced by 10%: the full price is days times `dailyPrice`, and
+  the total is that full price minus the discount.
+- A period of fewer than 3 days is priced as before (days times `dailyPrice`).
+- The discount is computed on the full price in euro cents and rounded to the nearest cent, halves rounding up,
+  so the total stays an integer. Example: 4 days at 1505 cents = 6020 full; discount 602; total 5418.
+  3 days at 1505 cents = 4515 full; discount 451.5 rounds to 452; total 4063.
+- `quote` and `book` return the reduced total. `book` returns the same total as `quote` for the same period.
+- `availability` and the booking-clash rules are unchanged.
+
+## Rules
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents (task-001 rule 1).
+2. Times are UTC midnights; a rental covers whole days (task-001 rules 2 and 3).
+3. This task supersedes task-001 rule 3 for periods of 3 or more days: their total is the discounted total above,
+   not days times `dailyPrice`. Periods shorter than 3 days keep the task-001 total.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: A 3-day period quotes the full price less 10%, rounded to the nearest cent (e.g. 7500 becomes 6750).
+- AC2: A period of 2 days or fewer quotes days times `dailyPrice`, with no discount (e.g. 2 days at 2500 is 5000).
+- AC3: A 4-day or longer period quotes the full price less 10%.
+- AC4: The discount rounds half up to the nearest cent, so the total is always an integer (e.g. 3 days at 1505
+  is 4063).
+- AC5: `book` returns the same discounted total as `quote` for the same period, for both short and long periods.
+- AC6: Existing error behaviour is unchanged: `quote` and `book` still throw for an unknown item or a period the
+  rules do not allow.
+
+## Notes
+
+- No runtime dependency is added. Tests use `node --test` (the existing `test` script).
+- Each acceptance criterion gets at least one happy-path test and one edge- or error-path test.
+- The existing test "returns the total as days times the daily price" uses a 3-day period and is updated to the
+  discounted total, as AC1 requires.
+- Cancellation remains out of scope, as in task-001.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Red first: five new or updated `quote` and `book` tests failed on the unchanged pricing, then passed once the
+  discount was added.
+- Implementation: `priceOf` in `src/index.ts` takes 10% off from `LONG_RENTAL_DAYS` (3) days on, rounding the
+  discount half up to the nearest cent. `quote` and `book` both price through it, so they agree.
+- `npm test`: 35 of 35 pass.
+- Not run: no type checker or linter is installed in this repository; `tsc` and an ESLint run were not available.
